  "body": "## Goal\n\nAdd a pure toolpath transform module in `crates/cl/src/cl/transform.rs` (re-exported by `camcraft-app`). Toolpath patterns, mirror folders, and nesting (`#2166`) share this module.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Translation (`translate`):** Shift every move, arc center, `Cycle`, `CompSpan`, `EdgeBreak`, and `PlasmaCut` by `(dx, dy, dz)`. Keep coordinates finite and snapped consistently with `crates/cl/src/cl/moves.rs` (`lattice`).\n- **2D XY rigid transform (`transform_xy`):** Rotate and translate a `Toolpath` in XY by `(tx, ty, angle_deg)` around a pivot. Rotate XY arc centers, cycles, compensation spans, and edge breaks. Flatten or refuse `XZ`/`YZ` vertical arcs clearly. Nesting (`#2166`) calls this function directly.\n- **3D rotary axis rotation (`rotate_about_axis`):** Rotate a `Toolpath` about an `A` (X) or `B` (Y) axis through an origin by `angle_deg`. Update `Move::axis` using `crates/cl/src/cl/frame.rs` (`TiltedFrame`) and `crates/cl/src/cl/pose.rs`. Flatten tilted arcs at `chord_tol`.\n- **Vertical-plane mirror (`mirror_plane`):** Reflect a `Toolpath` across a vertical plane (`nz == 0`).\n  - Refuse horizontal or tilted mirror planes by name (matching `crates/post/src/post/wcs_flip.rs`).\n  - Under `GeometricMirror`, reflect all coordinates and arc centers, invert `arc.ccw` (`G2` <-> `G3`), and swap `CompSide` (`G41` <-> `G42`), matching `crates/post/src/post/invert.rs` (RS-274 / ISO 6983).\n  - Under `PreserveClimb`, reverse planar cutting pass chains safely after entry and before retract (swapping lead-in and lead-out, keeping original `arc.ccw` and `CompSide`) for 2D contours, profiles, and chamfers. Refuse by name any path whose entry or engagement cannot reverse safely (helical ramps, adaptive clearing, multi-pass roughing).\n- **Refusals:** Return a named `TransformError` for unsupported records (turning `ThreadCycle`, `ProbeTouch`, tilted moves under mirror, non-finite inputs). Add no new crate dependencies.\n\n## Done means\n\nUnit tests in `crates/cl/` verify micron-accurate translation, XY rotation, A/B axis rotation, vertical-plane mirroring (`G2`/`G3` and `G41`/`G42` swap), safe 2D contour pass reversal under `PreserveClimb`, and named refusals for unsupported records and horizontal mirror planes.\n\nPart of #2938\n",
